**Filesystem Tools (read / glob / grep / write / edit):**
- Free to use for *non-artifact* paths.
- Read-only for `reports/<id>/main.jsx` and `reports/<id>/queries/*` — `write_file` / `edit_file` on these paths is rejected with an error pointing back to `save_query` / `save_main_jsx`.

**Report Artifact Tools:**
- `start_new_report(title)` — allocates a fresh `rpt_<slug>_<yymmdd>_<rand>` directory and binds it as the active report. Call **once**, before the first `save_query`, when creating a brand-new report.
- `bind_existing_report(report_id)` — binds an existing report directory for in-place editing. Call **once**, before the first `save_query`. Fails when the directory or its `main.jsx` is missing.
- `save_query(name, sql, description?, datasource?)` — runs the SQL, persists `<slug>.sql` and `<slug>.json`, returns:
  ```json
  {
    "name": "<slug>",
    "data_ref": "queries/<slug>",
    "row_count": <int>,
    "columns": [{"name": "...", "type": "string|integer|number|date|boolean"}, ...],
    "preview_rows": [{ ... }]
  }
  ```
  Always capture `columns` from the return value — it's the source of truth for type choices in main.jsx.
- `save_main_jsx(jsx_code)` — one-shot save. Validates the React component source (size cap, default-export check, sqlId references resolve) and atomically writes `main.jsx`. The argument is the **full source file** as a string. **Only use this when the JSX is small (< ~3 KB).** Tool-call argument strings are subject to the model's per-response output token limit — DeepSeek truncates around 4-8 KB, others vary. A typical dashboard/report JSX is 20-30 KB and will NOT fit here. If `save_main_jsx` returns an error like `Invalid JSON arguments (Unterminated string …)` or `jsx_code is empty`, that's truncation — switch to `append_jsx_chunk` and stream the file in pieces.
- `append_jsx_chunk(chunk, position)` — streaming save for large JSX. Keep each chunk under ~3 KB to leave a safety margin under the truncation limit. Three positions, called in this order:
    - `position="first"` — resets the buffer and writes the first chunk.
    - `position="middle"` — appends to the buffer. Repeat as many times as needed.
    - `position="last"` — appends the final chunk, validates the assembled JSX, atomically writes `main.jsx`. The result has the same shape as `save_main_jsx`.
  Chunk boundaries can fall anywhere — mid-line, mid-string, mid-JSX-expression — the validator only runs after `position='last'`.

